package types

// TraceDirectionEnvelopeOverlapTeaching explains legacy arithmetic markers
// without changing their wire values or granting a physical relation. Keep
// both pre-final token surfaces and the shared value teaching in sync.
const TraceDirectionEnvelopeOverlapTeaching = "`forbidden_by_typed_overlap` and `overlap_nonadditive` mean only that the published locator envelopes intersect, so the current subtotal is withheld. They do not establish physical overlap of the measured components; that requires independent exact interval-relation evidence."

// TraceRepairDirectionValueTeaching is shared soft guidance for consuming
// already-published Trace values. It neither computes aggregates nor grants
// evidence/answer authority. B1590a extracts the B1573 skill wording unchanged
// so the concentrated board cannot contradict the skill's arithmetic bounds.
const TraceRepairDirectionValueTeaching = "Within one direction, the largest seat's published value is the largest SINGLE ranked contribution, not that direction's total or recoverable ceiling. When an exact same-direction subtotal is published, use its own value and arithmetic caliber: it covers its listed members only, not an exhaustive direction total unless completeness is separately established. When only a leader is published or member relations are missing, keep the individual values and say that a direction total has not been established; do not replace the missing total with a maximum or infer additivity from a shared label. " + TraceDirectionEnvelopeOverlapTeaching + " Preserve the published estimate basis and bound direction: a supply-fold/head-room estimate is not an observed saving, and a published lower bound or conservative fallback must not become an upper bound or a guaranteed improvement."
